WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.290
Film Courage: Is there any mistake you made
early on in your career that you said “Never

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.290
again.”

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:08.300
And [the mistake] is not so much working with
someone or whatever.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:14.150
It’s something either you did or something
you didn’t pick up on about a situation

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.150
that cost you?

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.420
And you said “I will never…”

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:25.300
Bill Duke, Actor/Filmmaker/Author: I was offered
a role…I’m not going to tell you the role.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.640
It was a TV show.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:35.370
But I was paid to play this role that I did
not like and I think it’s an embarrassing

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.100
role of a bad guy.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:49.430
But I had been trying to get a job in TV for
like three years and couldn’t get anything.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:50.430
Rejection…rejection…rejection.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:01:00.170
So I find this role, I audition and I get
this role and friends of mine saw the script

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.250
and they said “Don’t do it.”

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:08.450
Totally broke, rent was due…maybe it will
give me something.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:17.289
I was on a hit TV show, too.

00:01:17.289 --> 00:01:20.279
I did it.

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:21.640
I did it.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.139
When I saw the footage I said “Oh my gosh!

00:01:25.139 --> 00:01:29.280
I hope nobody sees this.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:37.079
And maybe five to seven years later when I
had some real money I called the network and

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:45.659
tried to buy…[laughs] I tried to buy the
footage back that I was in, to try to buy

00:01:45.659 --> 00:01:47.869
the episode and I said I would pay whatever.

00:01:47.869 --> 00:01:48.880
They wouldn’t sell it to me.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.880
That’s how ashamed I was.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:58.939
But…I needed the money.

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:05.009
I needed the job…haven’t done it since
then.

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:11.680
But I understand see before I used to put
down the Stepin Fetchit, I used to put down

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:17.560
the people that came before me and smiled
and laughed and danced and acted like you

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:22.319
know happy black people and the maids and
butlers and stuff and “They are shaming

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:23.319
their race and…”

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:24.629
No, no, no.

00:02:24.629 --> 00:02:29.980
They took the jobs that were offered to them
at that time to do the best that they could

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:35.219
with what they had and my respect for them
changed totally because I was faced with the

00:02:35.219 --> 00:02:36.840
same thing.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.290
And I could understand why they did what they
did.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:46.519
But I was fortunate enough to not have to
do it again.

00:02:46.519 --> 00:02:52.390
I haven’t had to do it since.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:58.609
I still get these opportunities but to turn
down something that the gig can make you a

00:02:58.609 --> 00:03:07.140
lot of money, a lot of people would see but
it’s totally against everything you stand

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.700
for as an actor and artist and everything.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:17.879
I mean certain people put down certain people
because of what they did in a show or whatever

00:03:17.879 --> 00:03:20.010
and I don’t do that anymore.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:23.129
I just say you don’t know their circumstances.

00:03:23.129 --> 00:03:28.610
If you’ve got a sick baby at home, you’ve
got a sick baby at home.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:31.930
You’ve got to take care of your bills.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:35.080
I don’t know his business.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:40.150
I am not fond of reality TV though, I’m
not going to lie.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:51.540
I was out of the country and I was asked questions
about my culture based on reality TV and I

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.540
was saying

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:56.340
“No, that’s not the way every black person
in the world…not every black person’s

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:01.819
woman is dragged across the floor by their
hair.

00:04:01.819 --> 00:04:06.410
Not every black man wears his pants below
his butt line.”

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.980
[Imitates the questioner] “We thought all
blacks…?”

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:09.980
“No!”

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:13.959
“Because we were looking at your pants and
we were wondering why you didn’t have your

00:04:13.959 --> 00:04:14.959
pants..?”

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:19.690
Film Courage: Was this in Belgium when you
saw the one guy in the restaurant [referring

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.579
to a story he told earlier]?

00:04:21.579 --> 00:04:27.430
Nothing against Belgium but I was just wondering
if it was the same trip?

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:31.550
Bill: This was when I was in China years ago.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:32.800
I was in China.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:45.449
I was in Japan and in Tokyo and they just
said there was something wrong with me because

00:04:45.449 --> 00:04:49.230
I didn’t look like the regular black people.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:54.259
And he said “You speak good, too?”

00:04:54.259 --> 00:04:57.780
Film Courage: Did they know your work?

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:03.220
Bill: Some of them did.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:05.200
But at that time not a lot of them.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.920
They were just “Oh, you are hear filming?

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:07.920
Good.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:08.920
Good.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:10.030
I have some questions for you.”

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:21.990
I was in shock but not in a way because I
know the stuff that gets to them that’s

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:32.260
how they see us as a culture and I was just
amazed by how many people thought of us that

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.260
way.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.430
But media is very powerful.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:39.659
And that’s…whatever they see, that’s
what you are.

